From c2bcd63a0426df2dfcbf1ba9d1e402d6f77c16ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work_5_issue <adbtrr_work_5_issue@local>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] os/se/armino: fix bk7239n link failure on undefined
 bk_flash_get_protect_type

The secure storage wrapper added for the TP1X plus board calls
bk_flash_get_protect_type(). That API is only declared in
os/board/bk7239n/src/include/driver/flash.h and has no definition in the
in-tree Beken flash driver, where protection handling is limited to the
file-static helpers flash_set_protect_type()/flash_get_protect_cfg().

Because os/se/armino/Make.defs adds bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c whenever
CONFIG_SE_ARMINO=y, every bk7239n configuration fails at link time with:

  undefined reference to `bk_flash_get_protect_type'

Read the flash status register instead and test the block protection bits
directly. bk_flash_read_status_reg() is implemented in the flash driver and
FLASH_STATUS_BITS is already used by this file when writing the status
register, so the check stays self consistent. This mirrors the existing
Ameba implementation in os/se/ameba/rtl_security_api_wrapper_tz.c.

Verified by a full build of bk7239n/hello which now links tinyara.axf.
---
 os/se/armino/bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/os/se/armino/bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c b/os/se/armino/bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c
index 9f5ab8bd..3ec6058b 100644
--- a/os/se/armino/bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c
+++ b/os/se/armino/bk_security_api_wrapper_tz.c
@@ -123,12 +123,12 @@ int bk_ss_flash_read(uint32_t address, uint32_t len, uint8_t *data, int en_displ
   */
 int bk_verify_flash_protect(void)
 {
-	flash_protect_type_t protect_type;
+	uint16_t status_reg;
 
-	protect_type = bk_flash_get_protect_type();
-	printf("Flash Protect Type: %d\n", protect_type);
+	status_reg = bk_flash_read_status_reg();
+	printf("Flash Status Register: 0x%04x\n", status_reg);
 
-	if (protect_type != FLASH_PROTECT_NONE) {
+	if ((status_reg & FLASH_STATUS_BITS) == FLASH_STATUS_BITS) {
 		return 1;
 	} else {
 		return 0;
